    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "'mini.comment' [infers comment structure from 'commentstring' option](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1d49300d50a2c8ee7faecceb151084f207ff65ba/doc/mini-comment.txt#L11-L14). For me (and [by default](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/ea0737c838b029fc96b1321c4ac15e0dc7e29b84/runtime/ftplugin/markdown.vim#L15)) it is equal to `<!--%s-->` which is the same as the expected behavior.\r\n\r\nMy guess is that something overrides this to be `# %s`. It might be something trivial, like `FileType` autocommand or 'ftplugin/markdown.lua', either in the config or from plugin. Or it might be something less trivial: you use tree-sitter highlighting and have global 'commentstring' option set to `'# %s'` (which should be the default empty string `''` as [per documentation](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1d49300d50a2c8ee7faecceb151084f207ff65ba/doc/mini-comment.txt#L28-L30)).",
