        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Seems like you are right and the problem is related to treesitter, I'll just completely disable it with markdown files.\r\n\r\nIt seems to be too drastic, as allows massive quality of life improvement specifically in markdown (at least by highlighting code blocks with the language inside it, if it has tree-sitter highlighting enabled).\r\n\r\nI would suggest figuring out why 'commentstring' changes here. You can see the value of global option with `=vim.inspect(vim.go.commentstring)`. The aim is for it to output `\"\"`.",
